1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:04,350
I mean, I tried to stick them back on,
but before I could...

2
00:00:04,515 --> 00:00:09,225
(Howard:)...you turned into a giant loaf
of pumpernickel bread.

3
00:00:09,395 --> 00:00:10,855
(Howard:)What do you think that means?

4
00:00:12,273 --> 00:00:14,523
(Summer(uncomfortable):)I really don't know.

5
00:00:15,735 --> 00:00:17,115
(Howard:)I'll give you a little clue.

6
00:00:17,278 --> 00:00:20,698
My favorite sandwich?
Salami on pumpernickel.

7
00:00:21,615 --> 00:00:22,745
(Summer:)Is that so?

8
00:00:23,743 --> 00:00:27,533
Did you know the word pumpernickel comes
from the German words pumper and knickel.

9
00:00:27,705 --> 00:00:30,045
(Howard:)Which loosely translates to fart goblin?

10
00:00:31,917 --> 00:00:34,837
(Summer:)No. I didn't.

11
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:39,635
(Penny:)Okay, I found the box. Now what?

12
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:45,310
(Sheldon:)You're holding a Japanese puzzle box,
which takes 10 precise moves to open.

13
00:00:45,473 --> 00:00:48,723
Okay, first locate the
panel with the diamond pattern...

14
00:00:48,893 --> 00:00:52,603
...and slide the center portion
1 millimeter to the left.

15
00:00:52,772 --> 00:00:54,852
(Sheldon:)Then, on the opposite end of the box...

16
00:00:55,024 --> 00:00:58,154
(Sheldon:)...slide the entire panel
down 2 millimeters.

